# Paper-specific definitions and statements; no proofs or project Lean imports.
Import "../../library/Common.clean"

Source magnetic2025:
    Kind: other
    Label: Huang, Gleich, Li 2025
    Title: Powers of Magnetic Graph Matrix: Fourier Spectrum, Walk Compression, and Applications
    Author: Yinan Huang, David F. Gleich, Pan Li
    Version: arXiv:2506.07343v1
    Url: https://arxiv.org/html/2506.07343v1

Source magneticformalization:
    Kind: other
    Label: Clean magnetic formalization
    Title: Supporting results for the magnetic graph matrix
    Note: Supporting lemmas and conventions in studies/magnetic/Reference.lean

Define magnetic phase(q: Real): Complex:
    Equals: complex exponential(imaginary unit()*complex scalar(2*pi()*q))
    Render latex: e^{{2\pi i {q}}}

Define magnetic adjacency(A, q):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let q: Real
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Equals:
        magnetic phase(q)*complex matrix(A) +
        magnetic phase(-q)*complex matrix(real transpose(A))
    Render latex: M_{{{q}}}({A})

Define magnetic degree matrix(A):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Equals:
        complex matrix(diagonal(function(i: Vertex(n),
            sum vertices(function(j: Vertex(n), entry(A,i,j) + entry(A,j,i))))))
    Render latex: D({A})

Define magnetic Laplacian(A, q):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let q: Real
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Equals: magnetic degree matrix(A) - magnetic adjacency(A,q)
    Render latex: L_{{{q}}}({A})

# Every ordered word chooses one of the two directions at each position.
Define direction words(m: Natural): List(List(Boolean)):
    Equals: choices(repeat(m,pair(forward(),backward())))

Define word product(A,w):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let w: List(Boolean)
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Equals:
        ordered product(map(function(b: Boolean, choose(b,A,real transpose(A))),w))

Define walk profile(A, m, k):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let m: Natural
    Let k: Natural
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Equals:
        sum matrices(map(function(w: List(Boolean), word product(A,w)),
            filter(function(v: List(Boolean), count(forward(),v) = k),direction words(m))))
    Render latex: \Phi_{{{A}}}({m},{k})

Define walk Fourier sum(A, m, q):
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let m: Natural
    Let q: Real
    Returns: Matrix(n,n,Complex)
    Equals:
        magnetic phase(-(q*real index(m))) *
            sum before(m+1,function(k: Natural,
                magnetic phase(2*q*real index(k))*complex matrix(walk profile(A,m,k))))
    Render latex: e^{{-2\pi i {q}{m}}}\sum_{{k=0}}^{{{m}}}e^{{4\pi i {q}k}}\Phi_{{{A}}}({m},k)

Notation directed single edge(): Matrix(2,2,Real):
    Means: !![0, 1; 0, 0]
    Render latex: E_{{01}}



# All results here have proofs checked in Verified.lean.
# A is any real weighted matrix, with no symmetry or positivity assumption.
Result magnetic powers encode walk profiles:
    Attribution: magnetic2025; equation (1), Supplement S.II equation (17), Theorem 1; adapted; scope: forward transform only
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let m: Natural
    Let q: Real
    Conclude:
        magnetic adjacency(A,q)^m =
            magnetic phase(-(q*real index(m))) *
            sum before(m+1,function(k: Natural,
                magnetic phase(2*q*real index(k))*complex matrix(walk profile(A,m,k))))

Result magnetic adjacency is Hermitian:
    Attribution: magnetic2025; magnetic graph matrix definition; adapted
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let q: Real
    Conclude: Hermitian(magnetic adjacency(A,q))

Result magnetic Laplacian is Hermitian:
    Attribution: magneticformalization; unnormalized D minus M convention; direct
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Let q: Real
    Conclude: Hermitian(magnetic Laplacian(A,q))

Result zero potential symmetrizes adjacency:
    Attribution: magnetic2025; discussion following equation (1); adapted; scope: first power
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Conclude: magnetic adjacency(A,0) = complex matrix(A + real transpose(A))

Result two step mixed walk profile:
    Attribution: magnetic2025; walk profile examples preceding equation (1); adapted
    Let n: Natural
    Let A: Matrix(n,n,Real)
    Conclude:
        walk profile(A,2,1) =
            A*real transpose(A) + real transpose(A)*A

# In v1 equation (24), m = 1 leaves only the zero-potential term.
# The resulting half-symmetrization fails on a directed edge.
Result odd length inverse endpoint counterexample:
    Attribution: magneticformalization; inverse_v1_length_one_fails; direct; scope: v1 equation (24) at m = 1
    Conclude:
        complex matrix(walk profile(directed single edge(),1,1)) ≠
            complex scalar(1/2)*magnetic adjacency(directed single edge(),0)

